From: Philip John Basile <PBasile@Basilecom.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(mtp): fail closed on stateful logits processors

Native MTP evaluates draft and verifier distributions through separate calls.
An opaque stateful processor can therefore advance differently and invalidate
the acceptance calculation. Permit functions, functools.partial, and callables
that explicitly advertise `is_stateless=True`; reject unknown callable objects.

This patch is scoped to AirRunner/mlx-lm feat/mtp-native at
`e8ceeccf118d4a089e22431f28f89d5ffe7d9d2b`.

Source: ml-explore/mlx-lm#1740,
PhilipJohnBasile/mlx-lm@bc1d11414c12372cdf76538e09ce1fbc54b7fc7b

Signed-off-by: Philip John Basile <PBasile@Basilecom.com>
---
 mlx_lm/generate.py | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mlx_lm/generate.py b/mlx_lm/generate.py
--- a/mlx_lm/generate.py
+++ b/mlx_lm/generate.py
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 import argparse
 import contextlib
 import copy
+import inspect
 import json
 import math
 import sys
@@ -686,6 +687,22 @@ def mtp_generate_step(
     """
     validate_prompt_and_embeddings(model, prompt, input_embeddings)
 
+    if logits_processors:
+        unsafe_processors = [
+            type(processor).__name__
+            for processor in logits_processors
+            if not inspect.isfunction(processor)
+            and not isinstance(processor, partial)
+            and not getattr(processor, "is_stateless", False)
+        ]
+        if unsafe_processors:
+            names = ", ".join(unsafe_processors)
+            raise ValueError(
+                "Native MTP currently supports only stateless logits processors. "
+                "Use plain functions, functools.partial, or set is_stateless=True "
+                f"on a safe callable. Unsupported processor(s): {names}."
+            )
+
     y = prompt.astype(mx.uint32)
     prev_tokens = None
 
